  "description": "Governed Odoo ERP operations over the External API (JSON-RPC 2.0), spanning quote-to-cash, procure-to-pay, CRM, inventory, projects and document handling. Twenty-six commands: find, create, update and archive customers; find and create products and update their sales price; run a scoped read against any model and list accounting journals; draft a quotation, confirm it into a sales order, and cancel one; draft a customer invoice, post it to the ledger, email it to the customer, register a reconciled payment, and raise a credit note; draft vendor bills and purchase orders and confirm them; validate a delivery; create CRM leads and move them between stages; create project tasks; attach files to any record; and post internal notes to a record's chatter. Auth is a single Odoo 14+ API key in one vault entry, so the module never sees a user password. Every ledger-touching command runs write_requires_approval, and the irreversible ones re-read the live record and refuse when an approved total no longer matches.",
